mesa: let go of the fence a surface is flushed or processed again over

vlVaSurfaceFlush() (the upload of an image, the clear of a new surface) and the end of a
video-processing pass (vl_compositor_proc: the scale_vaapi of FFmpeg, the blit of
vaPutImage) flush into surf->pipe_fence, which gets the new fence of the flush and loses
the old one. The only places that let go of it are vaSyncSurface() and the destruction of
the surface, so a surface that is flushed again before a sync, which one of a pool is,
leaves the fence it had behind.

With virgl a fence owns a file descriptor: the sync_file that the kernel returns for the
out-fence of the execbuffer (VIRTGPU_EXECBUF_FENCE_FD_OUT), closed when the fence is freed.
The guest's KRDP kept one open for every frame it captured until it had 1024 of them,
after which every ioctl failed with EMFILE ("got error from kernel - expect bad rendering
24") and the picture froze.

Release the fence a flush is about to replace. The newer one covers it: both are fences of
the same context.

--- a/src/gallium/frontends/va/surface.c	2026-10-28 17:58:18.769410786 -0700
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/va/surface.c	2026-10-28 17:58:30.469583700 -0700
@@ -812,6 +812,14 @@
 void
 vlVaSurfaceFlush(vlVaDriver *drv, vlVaSurface *surf)
 {
+   /* A flush makes a new fence, which replaces the one in the surface: the one of the last flush
+    * is what vaSyncSurface waits for, and it is only let go of there and when the surface is
+    * destroyed. Replaced without a release, its fence is never freed, and with a driver whose
+    * fences hold a file descriptor (virgl: a sync_file) a surface that is flushed again and
+    * again, as the ones of a pool are, leaves one open a time until there are no more. */
+   if (surf->pipe_fence)
+      drv->pipe->screen->fence_reference(drv->pipe->screen, &surf->pipe_fence, NULL);
+
    drv->pipe->flush(drv->pipe, &surf->pipe_fence,
                     drv->has_external_handles ? 0 : PIPE_FLUSH_ASYNC);
 }
--- a/src/gallium/auxiliary/vl/vl_compositor_proc.c	2026-10-28 17:58:18.771011962 -0700
+++ b/src/gallium/auxiliary/vl/vl_compositor_proc.c	2026-10-28 17:58:30.814280800 -0700
@@ -185,8 +185,17 @@
                           struct pipe_picture_desc *picture)
 {
    struct vl_compositor_proc *proc = (struct vl_compositor_proc *)codec;
+   struct pipe_context *context = proc->b.context;
 
-   proc->b.context->flush(proc->b.context, picture->out_pipe_fence, picture->flush_flags);
+   /* out_pipe_fence is the pipe_fence of the target surface (vlVaEndPicture, vlVaPutImage), and
+    * the flush makes a new fence for it. The last one is what a sync waits for, so the one it
+    * replaces is let go of here: left, it is never freed, and with virgl its fence is a
+    * sync_file, one more of them open for every frame of a pooled surface that is processed
+    * again before it is synced. */
+   if (picture->out_pipe_fence && *picture->out_pipe_fence)
+      context->screen->fence_reference(context->screen, picture->out_pipe_fence, NULL);
+
+   context->flush(context, picture->out_pipe_fence, picture->flush_flags);
 
    return 0;
 }
